          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What kind of activity is described for someone with COPD who gets breathless walking?",
          "answer": "The retrieved guidance does not say what kind of activity is recommended for someone with COPD who gets breathless walking.\n\nThe COPD activity note (lifestyle-copd-activity) explains why exercise matters. Breathlessness makes people avoid activity, their muscles weaken, and the breathlessness then comes on sooner. It says the note is about \"what the activity consists of and how to keep it going,\" but the passage I received does not describe the activity itself. The full note may, but I cannot see it here.\n\nOther documents describe general activity, such as brisk walking or cycling, in the context of anxiety (lifestyle-generalized-anxiety-disorder-activity), high blood pressure (lifestyle-hypertension-activity), and type 2 diabetes (lifestyle-type-2-diabetes-activity). Those are not guidance for COPD, so I have not applied them here.\n\nA clinician, or a pulmonary rehabilitation programme if one is available, can advise on a safe type and amount of activity for a specific person. If breathlessness is severe, getting worse, or comes with chest pain or fainting, seek medical advice promptly.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
